P0 / P1 Defects Found & Fixed:
1. [P0-1][RESTART_RECOVERY / VOTE_ONCE_PER_TERM] RaftElectionService.simulateRestartAfterStop() & recoverFromStorage():
   - Issue: simulateRestartAfterStop() called state.becomeFollower(restoredTerm), which wiped persisted votedFor to null whenever durable storage term exceeded previous memory term, and did not reconcile/validate RaftState.restore(...) invariants (allowing double-vote across restart or silent acceptance of corrupt logs/checkpoints).
   - Fix: Added validateDurableState() enforcing term monotonicity, no term-0 vote, voter-only votedFor, and full RaftState.restore(...) invariants (fail-closed RaftStorageException). simulateRestartAfterStop() now faithfully restores persisted votedFor and fails closed on same-term memory/storage divergence.
2. [P0-2][VOTE_ONCE_PER_TERM] RaftElectionService.currentGrants & CandidateElection.handleRequestVote():
   - Issue: RaftElectionService maintained a separate currentGrants set updated before CandidateElection validated requestTerm == campaignTerm / activeCampaign() / partition isolation, and never cleared currentGrants on higher-term RequestVote step-down or leader-startElection precondition failure.
   - Fix: Exposed package-private CandidateElection.grantedVotersSnapshot() and clearCampaignOnStepDown() as single source of truth; RaftElectionService drops late replies from isolated peers, clears grants/ACKs on step-down and handleRequestVote term advances, checks Role.LEADER before mutating grants in startElection(), and guards grantedVoteCount()/hasWonElection() against FOLLOWER/stopped/failed states.
3. [P0-3][HIGHER_TERM_STEPDOWN] CandidateElection.startElection() synchronous re-entrant reply crash:
   - Issue: Calling voteRequestFor(expectedTerm).orElseThrow() inside the peer send loop threw NoSuchElementException and triggered failClosed() if a synchronous transport delivered a higher-term step-down or immediate 3/5 quorum win before the loop finished all 4 peers.
   - Fix: Guarded the peer loop with if (!activeCampaign()) break and Optional check before invoking transport.requestVote(); ordered EVENT_ELECTION_STARTED before synchronous EVENT_LEADER_ELECTED / EVENT_HIGHER_TERM_STEP_DOWN in RaftElectionService.termLog.
4. [P0-4][HIGHER_TERM_STEPDOWN] RaftElectionService fail-closed gap on RaftStorageException:
   - Issue: observeHigherTerm(), startElection(), handleRequestVote(), and transport vote callbacks did not set RaftElectionService.failed = true when storage persistence threw RaftStorageException.
   - Fix: Caught storage/runtime failures across all durable transitions in RaftElectionService, invoked failClosed() (clearing grants, campaign state, and peer ACKs), and rethrew.
5. [P0-5][QUORUM_SAFETY] WriteAvailabilityPolicy & RaftElectionService stale-term ACK reuse & partition propagation:
   - Issue: Peer ACKs were stored without term scoping (allowing term-1 ACKs to grant false 3/5 quorum in term 3 within freshnessWindow), accepted while FOLLOWER or from non-voters/future timestamps, and RaftElectionService.partition()/isolatePeer() did not mark isolated peers unresponsive in an attached WriteAvailabilityPolicy.
   - Fix: Scoped ACKs to TermedAck(term, timestamp) in both WriteAvailabilityPolicy and RaftElectionService, ignored non-leader/isolated ACKs, rejected future-dated ACKs and non-voter peerIds, cleared ACKs on term/role transitions, and propagated partition()/isolatePeer() directly to WriteAvailabilityPolicy.markPeerUnresponsive().
6. [P1-1][TIMER_RACES] ElectionRetryCoordinator.expire() double-arm race:
   - Issue: If startElection() synchronously triggered onValidAppendEntries/onVoteDecision (already arming a fresh deadline generation), expire() unconditionally called arm() again, cancelling the fresh timer.
   - Fix: Rearm in expire() only when generation == null.
7. [P1-2][TIMER_RACES] RaftElectionComponent shutdown race with late vote response:
   - Issue: Late vote responses arriving concurrently with RaftElectionComponent.close() called raw loop.execute(...) without catching RejectedExecutionException, falsely invoking onFailure.
   - Fix: Guarded with closed/failed checks and caught RejectedExecutionException when closed, matching execute(Runnable).
8. [P1-3][VOTE_ONCE_PER_TERM] RaftElectionService.auditTermLog():
   - Issue: auditTermLog() checked term monotonicity and at-most-one-leader-per-term, but did not audit vote-once-per-term across logged votedFor entries.
   - Fix: Added per-(nodeId, currentTerm) votedFor uniqueness check to auditTermLog().

